From: Box build <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: support Raspberry Pi kernel PL011 console

Raspberry Pi kernel device trees (6.12) give the BCM283x PL011 the
compatible "arm,pl011-axi" only. With the firmware passing that device
tree (OF_BOARD) and disable-bt making the PL011 serial0/stdout, no
driver matched the console node.

lists_bind_fdt() then returns 0 with *devp = NULL, and
serial_check_stdout() passed that NULL to device_get_uclass_id(),
crashing U-Boot before any output.

Match "arm,pl011-axi" in the BCM283x PL011 driver (same registers;
U-Boot already uses 32-bit accesses), and don't dereference a NULL
device when the stdout node has no driver.

--- a/drivers/serial/serial_bcm283x_pl011.c	2026-10-18 22:42:29.411357632 -0400
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial_bcm283x_pl011.c	2026-10-18 22:42:29.446647913 -0400
@@ -83,6 +83,8 @@
 
 static const struct udevice_id bcm283x_pl011_serial_id[] = {
 	{.compatible = "brcm,bcm2835-pl011", .data = TYPE_PL011},
+	/* Raspberry Pi kernel device trees name the BCM283x PL011 like this */
+	{.compatible = "arm,pl011-axi", .data = TYPE_PL011},
 	{}
 };
 
--- a/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c	2026-10-18 22:42:29.417398644 -0400
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c	2026-10-18 22:42:29.446938175 -0400
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 	 * anyway.
 	 */
 	if (node > 0 && !lists_bind_fdt(gd->dm_root, offset_to_ofnode(node),
-					devp, NULL, false)) {
+					devp, NULL, false) && *devp) {
 		if (device_get_uclass_id(*devp) == UCLASS_SERIAL &&
 		    !device_probe(*devp))
 			return 0;
